{
  "_doc": "The apps the runtime nav walk (1_cicd/src/cicd/test-nav-runtime.yml, driver 1_cicd/src/scripts/cloud-android-nav-walk.py) drives: every app on the shared nav libs. `ship` is its Ship workflow (the walk waits for that workflow's run of the same commit and tests the APK it built, else the APK on the rolling `latest` release), `artifact` the prefix of the APK artifact that run uploads, `asset` the release asset's base name (the walk prefers `<asset>-x86_64.apk`). An app on the shared bars that is not listed here is not walked: ChromeScrollGuardTest's app list and this one must name the same apps (the workflow's plan job fails otherwise). Optional per-app keys: `start_page` (\"mhtml\": the walk opens a deterministic local test page through a VIEW intent, no network, for an app whose home page is a live site); `walk_build` {dir, cmd, apk_glob} (the walk builds this APK itself in CI instead of taking the Ship APK, for a test-only variant that carries what the release never may, e.g. Mail's seeded offline account); `seed` (\"<receiver class>:<action>\", broadcast to the installed app before its first launch).",
